--TEST--
`Status::Draft` and `Config::MAX` are one production, so the checker's recorded resolution is what colours the case's own half and leaves the constant's silent — and what colours the name in front of each as the enum or the class it resolved to, `rule:ide/semantic-tokens-carry-the-qualifiers`, `rule:enums/no-class-machinery`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Status: int {
    case Draft = 1;
}
class Config { public const int MAX = 10; }
var $state = Status::Draft;
var $cap = Config::MAX;
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens
--EXPECT--
2:6+6 enum
3:10+5 enumMember
5:7+6 class
6:5+6 variable
6:14+6 enum
6:22+5 enumMember
7:5+4 variable
7:12+6 class
